From: OpenWrt MT6990 repair <mt6990@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: stop polling MT6990 fixed links

MT6990 uses fixed 2500base-x links. Polling an in-band status bit that this
PCS variant does not expose causes phylink to reconfigure and reset the
analog SerDes every second. Keep polling for all existing variants and turn
it off only for MT6990.

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -589,7 +589,7 @@ static struct phylink_pcs *mtk_pcs_lynxi
 	mpcs->xfi_tphy = serdes_phy;
 	mpcs->regmap = regmap;
 	mpcs->pcs.ops = &mtk_pcs_lynxi_ops;
-	mpcs->pcs.poll = true;
+	mpcs->pcs.poll = !is_mt6990;
 	mpcs->interface = PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_NA;
 	mpcs->flags = flags;
 	mpcs->fwnode = fwnode_handle_get(fwnode);
